[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to the use of MD5 hashing, which is susceptible to collision attacks. This vulnerability occurs because MD5 is considered insecure and can be exploited to generate different inputs that produce the same hash output, compromising the integrity and uniqueness of the hashed certificate. The reliance on MD5 instead of a more secure cryptographic hash function such as SHA-256 or SHA-3 introduces a risk of collision attacks, which could allow an attacker to forge certificates or manipulate data while maintaining the same hash value.

